From bc8074977d884e8d13eea9c3a8d979a6a6f78402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:56:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 38/51] coh: exclude GetAnchor work all-HWcc also does from
 check/wstart (build 74)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User decision (MOT1 v6 §3.1): C = only work all-HWcc does not do. The
hwcc flavor runs the same NR GetAnchor (NR=1 in every flavor: replica
sync to the log tail, replay, combining, index dispatch), so for one
anchor per section (read: the first attempt outside (A), sampled sections;
write: the final attempt, every section) the anchor is split with a
thread-local flag in nr waitstat:
- (i) index lookup = the hash-map dispatch -> ObjectThreadCoh.reserved[7]
  (lookup_ns_sampled, same sampled read sections as check_ns_sampled);
- (ii) the rest of the anchor minus Megalon-only flushes (replay flushes in
  exec_notify, log-entry clflush; scr only) minus (D) -> excluded too,
  reported outside CohSnap by rackobj::GetThreadAnchorSplit.
Megalon-only flushes inside the anchor stay in check. Observation only, no
protocol change. NR test for the flag; object-test checks the split.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
